{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Behold, my sheaf arose and also stood upright; and behold, your sheaves turned round about it.</b> The subject of the dream concerns sheaves, for it was shown to him that through sheaves and produce they would bow down to him. The sense of תְסֻבֶּינָה (\"they turned round about\") is that they would surround him like a king about to enter the courtyard, whose servants encamp all around him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:58.695541279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}